From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthew Schwartz <matthew.schwartz@linux.dev>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:59:03 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] DRMBackend: find HDR blocks in DisplayID 2 extensions

Some panels without a CTA-861 extension carry their HDR static metadata
and colorimetry blocks in a CTA-861 data block of a DisplayID 2
extension, as the ROG Xbox Ally X20's AMS740LS02 does. Only the CTA
extension is searched, so these panels report no HDR support even
though they advertise PQ and BT.2020.

Read both through libdisplay-info's di_info accessors, which need 0.2.0
and search DisplayID 2 from 0.4.0. Older releases keep the current
behavior.
